<section id="Sx2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Supplementary Material of Relational Pooling</h2>

</section>
<section id="S1a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">A </span>Tensor Representation and <math id="S1a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{vec}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>vec</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{vec}</annotation></semantics></math> Operation on Graphs</h2>

<div id="S1a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We briefly provide a concrete example of the representation of graphs and the operation <math id="S1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{vec}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>vec</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{vec}(G)</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider a graph with three vertices, one edge attribute at each edge, and two vertex attributes at each vertex. The connectivity structure and edge attributes are represented by the <math id="S1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 3\times 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 3\times 2</annotation></semantics></math> adjacency tensor <math id="S1a.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\mathsfit{A}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\mathsfit{A}}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S1a.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{(i,j,1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{(i,j,1)}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the value of the graph’s adjacency matrix and <math id="S1a.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{(i,j,2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{(i,j,2)}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the value of the additional edge attribute, <math id="S1a.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j\in V=\{1,2,3\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j\in V=\{1,2,3\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
